  "body": "Build cache instructions for direct cargo calls, and the release packaging build ignores any compiler wrapper (#935).\n\nWhat changed\n- One identical sentence in `.claude/skills/work-issue/SKILL.md`, `.claude/skills/resolve-conflicts/SKILL.md`, `.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md`, `.claude/agents/gate-runner.md`; AGENTS.md's build-cache paragraph says the same.\n- `cargo xtask release`: the packaging build (`build()`) removes `RUSTC_WRAPPER` and `CARGO_BUILD_RUSTC_WRAPPER` from the cargo child's environment (`exec::packaging_env_clear`, a pure function). The release gate tier may still use the cache.\n- Not touched: `.cargo/config.toml`, `.claude/settings.json`.\n- Also collapsed one nested `if` in `exec::cache_env` that the current clippy rejects (no behaviour change).\n\nTests: `cargo test -p xtask` 33 passed (new: `packaging_build_clears_compiler_wrappers`); `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean; `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main --dry-run` plans xtask unit tests only. Not exercised: a real `cargo xtask release`.\n\nPROCESS_VERSION 16. A fork must pull the process files.\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #935\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
